# Lock accounting period

## UI text

`Lock accounting period` → `Period 2025-07 is still open for edits.`

Means: month **`2025-07`** (July 2025) is **not locked**. Users can still edit/delete/reclassify transactions dated in that month.

## What lock does

When a period is **locked** (`isLocked`):

- Edits to dates/amounts/categories in that month are blocked (or require unlock)
- Protects figures used for BAS / year-end packs from accidental change
- Month-End checklist marks the lock task **done**

When **open** (current message):

- Normal editing allowed
- Checklist shows this as a remaining / blocking item until locked

## July 2025 empty

Default checklist month is often **calendar/default** (e.g. 2025-07). If bank activity is Apr–Jun 2026:

- July 2025 with “no bank lines” is expected
- Lock July only if you truly finished that empty month, or **change Period** to a month that has statements before locking

## SELPIC cash workflow

- Lock **after** categorisation + bank reconcile for months that have data
- Do not treat “still open” on an empty July as an error in FY P&L
- Unlock only when a deliberate correction is needed

## Code

- Checklist copy: `lib/subledger/month-end-checklist.ts` (`lock-period` task)
- Enforcement: `lib/period-management/period-lock.ts` / period storage `isLocked`
